ENTRY            D6451   20260820   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D6451001   20260820   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 10         29
TITLE      Understanding the low-energy incomplete fusion
            reactions
AUTHOR     (A.Yadav, G.Ram, M.Shariq Asnain, I.Majeed, M.Shuaib,
            V.R.Sharma, I.Bala, U.Gupta, S.Gupta, D.P.Singh,
            P.P.Singh, M.K.Sharma, R.Kumar, B.P.Singh, R.Prasad)
INSTITUTE  (3INDMUA,3MEXUMX,3INDNSD,3INDIIR,3INDLUL)
           (3INDIND) Jamia Millia Islamia, New Delhi
           (3INDIND) Amity University, Noida
           (3INDIND) Agra College, Agra
           (3INDIND) University of Petroleum and Energy Studies,
            Dehradun
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,107,044605,2023)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.107.044605
FACILITY   (VDGT,3INDNSD)
SAMPLE     Isotopically pure, self-supporting targets of 159Tb
            of thickness ~0.98 to 2.00 mg/cm2 and the aluminum
            catcher and energy degrader foils of thickness ~1.6
            to 2.6 mg/cm2 prepared by rolling technique.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) Energy resolution 2.0 keV for the 1.33 MeV
            gamma-ray of 60Co.
METHOD     (STTA,ACTIV) Four stacks, each containing three
            target-catcher foil assemblies, were irradiated for
            8-10 h.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) The cumulative error, including statistical
            uncertainties, is estimated to be <15%
           (ERR-1) thickness of target foils (~1%)
           (ERR-2,,2.) geometry detector efficiency (<2%)
HISTORY    (20260802R) Data received from A.Yadav
           (20260820C) A.Gandhi
ENDBIB              29
COMMON               1          3
ERR-1
PER-CENT
         1.
ENDCOMMON            3
